 "decisions": [
  "Preserved attributes byte-for-byte: apply.py replaces only the [body_start, body_end) span of <string>/<item> elements; element names, order, indentation, CRLF line endings and every attribute (notably formatted=\"false\" on 107 strings) are untouched.",
  "Self-closing elements (e.g. <string name=\"common_empty\" />) are skipped by a real tag scanner; a naive regex (the one in build-cache.mjs) mis-parses it and produces one bogus cache key.",
  "aapt2 does NOT collapse '%%': the pristine resources.arsc stores '%%' verbatim in 43 values. Therefore a literal percent is doubled ONLY in genuine format strings (source had format args, where String.format turns '%%' back into '%'); plain strings such as 'battery below 20%' keep a single '%' so the UI does not show '%%'.",
  "Placeholders: positional indices are preserved; when MT reorders or changes conversions, each English specifier is mapped back to the source argument by conversion type (so a %s String arg is never formatted with %d), and 2+ specifiers are emitted positionally because aapt2 rejects multiple non-positional substitutions.",
  "Apostrophes are always escaped as \\' (aapt2 rejects a bare apostrophe); odd quote runs are made literal with \\\" so aapt2 never reports an unterminated quote; & < > are XML entities; control characters are stripped; a leading @ or ? is escaped as \\@ / \\? so it is not parsed as a resource reference; existing <u> markup is kept as markup (aapt2 compiles it to a style span).",
  "Context-sensitive values are translated by resource name/position, never by a global map: week_day = Sunday..Saturday; date_unit_list = Year/Month/Day; time_unit_list = Hour/Minute/Second; weekday_picker_*/share_select_week_day_* = Mon..Sun; common_month/月 = Month (not 'moon'); common_minute/分 = Min (not 'point'); SimpleDateFormat patterns (yyyy年MM月dd日 etc.) are rewritten as real English patterns because MT words would be misread as pattern letters.",
  "Fullwidth CJK punctuation is normalised to ASCII in English values (IP： -> IP:, 【X】 -> [X], ￥ -> ¥): MT keeps CJK punctuation code points around English text, which are not Chinese characters but would look wrong and keep an audit at 'zero CJK-ish chars' from passing.",
  "formatted=\"false\" only disables aapt2's compile-time format validation, NOT runtime String.format; those 107 strings therefore still go through specifier reconciliation (but never have literal % doubled). Verified with a Java-String.format simulator over all 966 translated format strings: 0 unsafe (no numeric conversion on a String arg, no missing arg, no bare %).",
  "apktool 3.0.3 removed the -s/--no-src flag ('Unrecognized option: -s'). A plain `apktool b` was used instead; this version automatically copies the raw classes.dex..classes5.dex from the decoded tree ('I: Copying raw classes*.dex...'), so the rebuilt APK carries the original vendor dex. The build script checks the zip afterwards and only re-adds dex entries if apktool ever omits them.",
  "The build tree is the Lead's decoded orig-res tree (patched in place); no other part of the tree was modified, so resource IDs are unchanged (public.xml untouched) - the 'Missing required view with ID' failure mode from the earlier full rebuild cannot be triggered by this change surface."
 ]
